lesson: 201
title: Legs on insects and spiders
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.
explain: A spider is not an insect: it has 8 legs.
explain: To count the legs, multiply each kind by its legs and add: 3 spiders and 4 beetles have 3 × 8 + 4 × 6 = 24 + 24 = 48 legs.
vars: a=name b=name s=2..9 n=2..12
answer: 8 * s + 6 * n
exercise: A jar holds {s} spiders and {n} beetles. How many legs are there in the jar?
exercise: {a} finds {s} spiders and {n} ants under a stone. How many legs do they have altogether?
exercise: In the garden {a} counts {n} ladybirds on the roses and {s} spiders in their webs. How many legs is that in all?
exercise: There are {n} grasshoppers and {s} spiders in the long grass. How many legs do they have together?
exercise: {a} and {b} catch {n} beetles and {s} spiders for the class bug hotel. How many legs live in the bug hotel?
exercise: How many legs do {s} spiders and {n} bees have altogether?
exercise: got {s} spiders n {n} ants in the jar lol how many legs is that
exercise: {s} spiders in the shed, {n} beetles too, oh and the door's broken again. how many legs all up
exercise: theres {n} ladybirds, no wait {n+1}... no {n}, and {s} spiders on the window. legs?
exercise: my sis caught {n} grasshoppers and {s} spiders, she's well proud. how many legs they got
exercise: {a} reckons a spider has 6 legs like the beetles. nah. {s} spiders and {n} beetles, how many legs then
test: The legs of {n} ants and {s} spiders are counted together. What total do you get?
test: Under the log {b} spots {s} spiders, and next to them {n} beetles scuttle about. Count all their legs.
test: {n} bees buzz round the picnic while {s} spiders hang from the tree above. Find the number of legs.
test: What is the total number of legs on a shelf of jars holding {s} spiders and {n} grasshoppers?
test: {a} drew {n} ladybirds and {s} spiders and gave every one of them the right number of legs. How many legs did {a.he} draw?
test: how many legs on {n} ants + {s} spiders
test: {s} spiders and like {n} beetles in the bucket, my brother's screaming. legs total??
exam: Determine the aggregate number of legs possessed by a collection comprising {s.words} spiders and {n.words} beetles.
exam: It is given that a glass receptacle contains {s} spiders and {n} ants. Ascertain the total quantity of legs present therein.
exam: A survey of a garden records {n} ladybirds and, in addition, {s} spiders. Compute the total number of legs pertaining to all specimens so recorded.
exam: Pursuant to an inspection of a bug hotel, {s} spiders and {n} grasshoppers were enumerated. State the combined number of their legs.
exercise: {a}'s jar had {s+1} spiders and {n} beetles, but one spider 'went to live on a farm' (it got out). How many legs are in the jar now?
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} his insect cases: {s} spiders and {n} beetles, all pinned. How many legs are in the cases?
